"This code, as well as the previous one, generates a file called COLVAR with "
"the value of the CVs. All plumed files begin with a head that describes the "
"fields that it contains. In this case, the heading looks like:"
msgstr ""

#: README.md:307
msgid ""
"As you can see, the first column corresponds to the time, the second one is "
"the second central moment (SCM) and the third column is the third central "
"moment (TCM). When we plot this trajectory in the space of this CVs (that "
"is, the second and third columns) we obtain this result:"
